// SH28: AOT image exec is an OS-spawned process — policy "aot-process" is true.
// import "kab/noll/noll_aotproc"
// Evidence: kab/aot/aot_proc `aotProcExecOk` runs the entry-resolved image
// under an os_spawn'd pid (own process-table entry + own VA space), guest
// rax == Kab mirror (sh28_aot_proc_exec_smoke). A REAL OS-process leg now
// exists too: `aotNativeProcExecOk` spawns `kabootar exec-image` through
// run_command and the child maps+jumps into the image's machine code
// (sh28_aot_native_exec_smoke). The exec-image verb also takes a real i64
// argument across the host ABI (win64/sysv variants emitted honestly —
// abi:mismatch refused), so runtime input now crosses process argv AND the
// ABI boundary into image code. nollImageIsProcess and nollMmapExecProcess
// stay false — the image/mmap are still not processes themselves.
// Do not grow noll_proc.kab or noll_aot.kab. Do not delete src/. nollAotReady stays false.

pub fn nollAotProcess() {
    return true
}
